  "overview": {
    "title": "Dates, produce and local pace",
    "p1": "Zagora’s souk is a working market, not a polished tourist bazaar. On market days the town fills with produce, dates, household goods and the rhythm of the wider Draa.",
    "p2": "Come early for the best atmosphere. It is a place to watch and buy practical things more than to hunt for high-end crafts — Tamegroute remains stronger for pottery.",
    "p3": "Keep valuables close and enjoy the ordinary energy of a southern oasis market."
  },
